# Applications in School Mathematics: 1979 Yearbook.

**Authors:** Sharron, Sidney, Ed., Reys, Robert E., Ed.

## Abstract
Presented are twenty essays related to applications in school mathematics and aimed at the classroom teacher. The essays use numerous examples and illustrations that provide the teacher with something tangible for immediate use. Four thematic areas are addressed: (1) What are applications?; (2) Why include applications in school mathematics?; (3) How can applications be brought to the classroom?; and (4) What issues are related to applications? Topics covered include direct word quotes, human variability, finance, music, environmental problems, socioeconomic problems, and statistics. (MP)

